Subject: [Krypton] Monochrome Chromium Settings in light and dark mode

The user requested a Vercel-style black-and-white Settings page rather than
Helium's accent-colored WebUI. Scope neutral color tokens to Settings and
restyle its existing cards, navigation and search field. Keep native control
behavior, semantic error colors, and system high-contrast colors. Use local
fonts without network requests. All resources already exist, so no GRIT IDs,
browser C++ changes, or native KryptonUI changes are needed.

--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/settings.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/settings.html
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 <!doctype html>
-<html dir="$i18n{textdirection}" lang="$i18n{language}" class="loading"
+<html krypton-settings-theme dir="$i18n{textdirection}" lang="$i18n{language}" class="loading"
     $i18n{webuiRefresh2026} $i18n{settingsRefresh2026} $i18n{roundedIconsAttribute} $i18n{webuiRoundedIconsAttribute}>
 <head>
   <meta charset="utf-8">
@@ -39,7 +39,22 @@
       font-family: 'Google Sans', Roboto, sans-serif;
     }
 </if>
-  </style>
+  
+    /* Krypton monochrome: paint the requested scheme before modules load. */
+    @media (forced-colors: none) {
+      html[krypton-settings-theme],
+      html[krypton-settings-theme][webui-refresh-2026],
+      html[krypton-settings-theme][settings-refresh-2026] {
+        background: light-dark(#fff, #000);
+        color: light-dark(#171717, #ededed);
+      }
+
+      html[krypton-settings-theme] body {
+        font-family: 'Geist', 'Segoe UI Variable Text', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
+      }
+    }
+
+    </style>
 </head>
 <body>
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="chrome://resources/css/text_defaults_md.css">
